Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:53:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 343/638] media: provide Chrome key-system observer on AROS

Compile the portable Chrome renderer key-system observer on AROS so CEF's renderer client can register CDM support without an unresolved GetChromeKeySystems seam.

AI_PHASE: chromium-shared-cef

AI_STATUS: exact-link-gap-fixed-under-validation

AI_VALIDATION: registered native link contained exactly one unresolved GetChromeKeySystems symbol

AI_LIMITATIONS: CDM runtime behavior and CEF native link remain pending

AI_EVIDENCE: aros-opal-hosted-clean/test-artifacts/-cef-zero-v8-native-link-20260725/04-undefined-symbols.txt

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:
---
 chrome/renderer/BUILD.gn | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/renderer/BUILD.gn b/chrome/renderer/BUILD.gn
index fd99154d77..34e13eacf6 100644
--- a/chrome/renderer/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/renderer/BUILD.gn
@@ -313,7 +313,7 @@ static_library("renderer") {
     deps += [ "//third_party/widevine/cdm:headers" ]
   }
 
-  if (enable_library_cdms || is_win || is_android) {
+  if (enable_library_cdms || is_win || is_android || is_aros) {
     sources += [
       "media/chrome_key_systems.cc",
       "media/chrome_key_systems.h",
